Zucchini keeps reference locations, targets and equivalences in std::deque. Chromium builds
against libc++, whose deque blocks hold 4 KiB; MSVC's hold 16 bytes, so sorting and searching
millions of offsets pays for an allocation and an indirection every few of them. std::vector
gives byte-identical patches and results, at the cost of contiguous allocations and some peak
memory while a vector grows.

